 to derive if we fix  the value of K this is a density and  therefore it must integrate to one so  the integral of this ratio with respect  to Y has to be equal to 1 now there's no  y in the denominator so the integral of  the numerator divided by the denominator  has to be equal to 1 which means that  the denominator must be equal to the  integral of the numerator when we  integrate over all Y's and this is just  what this expression is saying so what  we will do next will be to consider one  example for each one of these two cases  of the Bayes rule that we have just  derived
 

